cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  MorphoFavela — Morphometric analysis of informal settlements:
  CFD-coupled analysis of pedestrian-level wind, solar, and ventilation
  in Rio de Janeiro favelas
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below.
  An accompanying journal article is in preparation; this CITATION
  file will be updated with its DOI once published.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hermann
    given-names: Theo
    email: thermann.ai@gmail.com
    affiliation: >-
      Massachusetts Institute of Technology
repository-code: 'https://github.com/thrmnn/MorphoFavela'
abstract: >-
  MorphoFavela is a Python pipeline for analysing the morphometry, environmental
  performance, and CFD-derived ventilation of informal settlements. It
  combines GIS-based building/terrain extraction, sky-view-factor and
  solar-access computation, stratified CFD patch sampling (119 patches
  across 5 Rio de Janeiro favelas), and an ingestion layer for
  OpenFOAM-derived wind fields. The framework is being applied to
  Vidigal, Rocinha, Complexo do Alemão, Rio das Pedras, and Maré to
  quantify pedestrian-level wind, ventilation, and solar exposure as
  drivers of climate vulnerability in dense informal urban form.
keywords:
  - urban morphometry
  - informal settlements
  - favela
  - sky view factor
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - CFD
  - urban climate
  - ventilation
  - Rio de Janeiro
  - GIS
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-04-13'
